# Division, remainder and right shift read their operand as their type:
# a negative number's quotient and remainder are machine-dependent (PTX
# ISA §9.7.1.10) and an unsigned shift fills with zeros (§9.7.8.9), so
# div.u32, shr.u32 and rem.s32 of a value that may be negative are
# refused, and shr.s32 of a value above the s32 range: each store's
# address is unknown with that reason. shr.s32 by 31 of the constant −5
# is −1: the store is at param_0 − 4, one sector per warp request.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/division_operands.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store addr ? (`div.u32` of a value that may be negative){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store addr ? (`shr.u32` reads a value its type does not hold){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store addr ? (`rem.s32` of a value that may be negative){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store addr ? (`shr.s32` reads a value its type does not hold){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store [param_0 - 4] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
